+// The two phases that can plausibly own a 1.2 second frame, so that
+// total - gcode - swap leaves everything else with nowhere to hide.
+//
+// A preview frame measured 41 ms at rest and 1173 ms while being touched, on
+// the same 2.4 million segment scene, with the picking pass measured at zero.
+// Those two numbers have different fixes: if the toolpath draw owns it, the
+// scene has to get smaller or be drawn less often; if the swap owns it, the
+// GPU is simply behind and the cost is backpressure, which is fixed by
+// submitting less rather than by drawing differently.
+std::atomic<uint64_t> orca_ios_canvas_gcode_us{0};
+std::atomic<uint64_t> orca_ios_canvas_swap_us{0};
 
